From 41aaa11815a9d67f67e7f10c8e95bd8c8805b902 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mechres <164776284+Mechres@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 01:31:06 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] ARM: dts: sun6i: exper-t8e: Give the cpu nodes a capacity

The four Cortex-A7 cores are identical, but without capacity-dmips-mhz
the ARM topology code wants a clock-frequency property in each cpu node
and logs "missing clock-frequency property" four times at every boot.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 .../dts/allwinner/sun6i-a31s-exper-t8e.dts    | 21 +++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 21 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm/boot/dts/allwinner/sun6i-a31s-exper-t8e.dts b/arch/arm/boot/dts/allwinner/sun6i-a31s-exper-t8e.dts
index 6f2366ebf..3a6ccf500 100644
--- a/arch/arm/boot/dts/allwinner/sun6i-a31s-exper-t8e.dts
+++ b/arch/arm/boot/dts/allwinner/sun6i-a31s-exper-t8e.dts
@@ -28,6 +28,27 @@ wifi_pwrseq: pwrseq {
 	};
 };
 
+/*
+ * All four cores are identical Cortex-A7. Without a capacity the ARM topology
+ * code expects a clock-frequency property in every cpu node and prints
+ * "missing clock-frequency property" for each core.
+ */
+&cpu0 {
+	capacity-dmips-mhz = <1024>;
+};
+
+&cpu1 {
+	capacity-dmips-mhz = <1024>;
+};
+
+&cpu2 {
+	capacity-dmips-mhz = <1024>;
+};
+
+&cpu3 {
+	capacity-dmips-mhz = <1024>;
+};
+
 /* PH21 (UART0 RX) is floating — adapter only has RX<->TX
  * and GND connected; crosstalk from TX signal generates ghost DR bit.
  * Adding pull-up to RX pin. */
-- 
